  "body": "> When designing APIs that create and return a buffer, it is recommended to use the ArrayBuffer type rather than Uint8Array.\r\n\r\nWe do this in Fetch on `Request` and `Response` objects, but we do not do it inside streams. The Encoding Standard also does not do this. I wonder how sound this advice is.\r\n\r\n> When designing APIs that take a buffer, it is recommended to use the BufferSource typedef rather than ArrayBuffer or any of the view types.\r\n\r\nThis is generally still true, but it's not true when the API ends up writing into it. In that case the Encoding Standard decided to use Uint8Array. We might want to cover that separately.",
